# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` — the default from Git for Windows'
# installer, and what this machine is set to — rewrites line endings to CRLF on
# checkout. Biome's formatter defaults to LF and rejects the whole file, so a
# plain `git checkout <file>` is enough to turn a clean working tree into a
# failing lint. That happened during Slice 3: reverting one file made biome
# fail on it, and the fix looked like a content change when nothing about the
# content had changed.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git decide what is text and leave binaries alone;
# `eol=lf` pins the working-tree ending so the repo, the formatter and CI all
# agree.
* text=auto eol=lf
